CE FND-129 guardrail: TWO current sources, which fnec must refuse.
CE Two parallel half-wave elements, each asking for 1 A at its centre.
CE fnec drives only the first: solve_current_source_hallen picks its source
CE with a find_map over the EX cards, pins the current at that one segment
CE and returns one port voltage.
CE Measured before the refusal, exit 0 with no warning at all: BOTH feedpoint
CE rows printed the same voltage 42.004192 -j121.198169, which is the first
CE source's port voltage, while row 2's current came out -0.250051 -j0.311050
CE instead of the 1 A requested -- induced current from the other element, so
CE the second source was never impressed. Its reported 170.74 +j272.30 ohm was
CE a wrong voltage over a current nobody drove.
GW 1 21 0 0 -5.0 0 0 5.0 0.001
GW 2 21 3.0 0 -5.0 3.0 0 5.0 0.001
GE
EX 4 1 11 0 1.0 0.0
EX 4 2 11 0 1.0 0.0
FR 0 1 0 0 14.2 0.0
